  "text_pages": [
    "Housing Benefits - International Welcome e-desk - University of Strasbourg\nShare the page :\nAdd the page to your favorites :\nPage has been added to favorites\nPage has been removed from favorites\nHousing Benefits\nHousing benefits allow you to:\nPay your deposit\n(Visale and Loca Pass guarantees);\nHelp with your rent\n(Apl, Alf, Als);\nFinance part of your move\n​​​​​​​(one-off assistance for employees of the University of Strasbourg).\nThese aids are subject to conditions.\nThe Visale guarantee allows you to\nhave a reliable and trustworthy guarantor free of charge\n. Set up by the French government, this aid is aimed at\nyoung people aged between 18 and 30 and employees aged over 30 (subject to conditions).\nVisale Guarantee\nVisale Guarantee tutorial\nThe Loca Pass\n—\nAction Logement\noffers a\n0% interest loan to pay your deposit\n, which is usually required when you sign your lease.\nThis guarantee is\nsubject to conditions.\nLoca - Pass\nSome financial aids offered by the French government are made to reduce the price of rent. In order to benefit from them, you must have a valid permit of residence and your profile must match their ressources conditions.\n3 types of financial aid:\nAide personnalisée au logement (Apl)\n—\nPersonalised housing benefit\nAllocation de logement familiale (Alf)\n—\nFamily housing benefit\nAllocation de logement sociale (Als)\n—\nSocial housing benefit\nPersonalised housing assistance\nRunning a simulation or applying for housing benefit\nLe budget 2026 du gouvernement français restreint l'accès aux APL à partir du 1er juillet 2026.\nQui est concerné ?\nLes étudiants qui remplissent les deux conditions suivantes :\nne pas être originaire d'un pays de l'Union européenne, de l'Espace économique européen (EEE) ou de Suisse ;\nne pas être boursier sur critères sociaux (y compris s'ils disposent d'un visa long séjour VLS-TS).\nCette mesure ne concerne pas :\nles étudiants originaires de l'Union européenne, de l'Espace économique européen (EEE) ou de Suisse ;\ntous les étudiants boursiers sur critères sociaux, quelle que soit leur nationalité.\nSource officielle :\nMinistère de l'Enseignement supérieur et de la Recherche\nIf you are a staff member of the University of Strasbourg, you may,\nunder certain conditions\n(in particular the length of your contract and your household resources),\nbe entitled to a one-off financial contribution towards the cost of moving\nonce you have signed your tenancy agreement.\nMore information on the SPACS website\nMenu\nBrowse those links to navigate the website\nDisplay\nHide\nthe searchbox\nFill in your search :\nLaunch search\nClose\nOur audiences :\nStudent Profile\nResearcher Profile\nI think about it\nBefore\nmy arrival\nI am\nin\nStrasbourg\nBefore\nmy departure\nServices Pack"
  ],
